    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Someone and something",
     "texto": [
      "**Quelqu'un** (someone) and **quelque chose** (something) are used in affirmative sentences: **Il y a quelqu'un au bureau** (there is someone in the office).",
      "**Tu veux quelque chose ?** (do you want something?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Everyone",
     "texto": [
      "**Tout le monde** (everyone) takes a singular verb: **Tout le monde aime le café** (everyone likes coffee).",
      "Remember: **personne** (nobody) is the opposite of **quelqu'un** and goes with **ne**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
